            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A surge suppression module (706) comprises an elongated enclosure (730) configured to insert longitudinally into a chassis (702) of a surge suppression unit (700) and multiple surge suppression devices (100A, 100B, 100C, 100D) attached end-to-end and extending longitudinally within the elongated enclosure (730). The module (706) also comprises bus bars (742A, 742B, 742C, 742D) having a first end connected to one of the surge suppression devices (100A, 100B, 100C, 100D), a middle section extending to a back end of the enclosure (730), and a second end; as well as connectors (734A, 734B, 734C, 742D) connected to the second end of the bus bars (742A, 742B, 742C, 742D) and configured to slidingly connect to a connection panel (704) when the enclosure (730) is inserted into the chassis (702).</p>
            </abstract>
